--- !u!114 &1787637679444441036
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5992915200534118724}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Clownfish are small marine fish that live in warm shallow waters, particularly
    in coral reefs. They are best known for their mutualistic relationship with sea
    anemones - clownfish gain protection from predators by living among the anemone\u2019s
    stinging tentacles, while the anemone benefits from the clownfish cleaning away
    debris and attracting food. Clownfish communicate through soft popping or clicking
    sounds.\n\nFun Fact: Clownfish can change sex, and the dominant individual in
    a group becomes the breeding female."
